Subject: [PATCH] Keep firmware queue statistics out of the host skb queue

qdisc->q.qlen belongs to the Linux skb list and controls scheduler emptiness.
Writing a firmware queue length there can hide a queued skb or underflow
the count when the host dequeues it. Hardware queue length is already
reported separately through qstats->qlen and the NSS stats dump wrapper.

--- a/nss_qdisc/nss_qdisc_stats.c
+++ b/nss_qdisc/nss_qdisc_stats.c
@@ -389,7 +389,6 @@ static void nss_qdisc_stats_process_node_stats(struct nss_qdisc *nqr,
 		bstats = &qdisc->bstats;
 		qstats = &qdisc->qstats;
 		refcnt = &qdisc->refcnt;
-		qdisc->q.qlen = response->sn_stats.qlen_packets;
 	}
 
 	/*
